{"id":"ramoth-gilead","name":"Ramoth-Gilead","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:ramoth-gilead"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Ramoth-gilead","text":"Heights of Gilead, a city of refuge on the east of Jordan; called “Ramoth in Gilead” (Deut. 4:43; Josh. 20:8; 21:38). Here Ahab, who joined Jehoshaphat in an endeavour to rescue it from the hands of the king of Syria, was mortally wounded (1 Kings 22:1-36). A similar attempt was afterwards made by Ahaziah and Joram, when the latter was wounded (2 Kings 8:28). In this city Jehu, the son of Jehoshaphat, was anointed by one of the sons of the prophets (9:1, 4). It has with probability been identified with Reimun, on the northern slope of the Jabbok, about 5 miles west of Jerash or Gerasa, one of the cities of Decapolis. Others identify it with Gerosh, about 25 miles north-east of es-Salt, with which also many have identified it. (See RAMATH-MIZPEH.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H7433","lemma":"רָמֹת גִּלעָד","xlit":"Râmôth Gilʻâd","gloss":"Ramoth-Gilad, a place East of the Jordan","kjv":"Ramoth-gilead, Ramoth in Gilead. See also H7216","count":7,"share":0.26},{"strong":"H758","lemma":"אֲרָם","xlit":"ʼĂrâm","gloss":"Aram or Syria, and its inhabitants","kjv":"Aram, Mesopotamia, Syria, Syrians","count":9,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H2371","lemma":"חֲזָאֵל","xlit":"Chăzâʼêl","gloss":"Chazael, a king of Syria","kjv":"Hazael","count":6,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H3092","lemma":"יְהוֹשָׁפָט","xlit":"Yᵉhôwshâphâṭ","gloss":"Jehoshaphat, the name of six Israelites","kjv":"Jehoshaphat","count":5,"share":0.19},{"strong":"H3141","lemma":"יוֹרָם","xlit":"Yôwrâm","gloss":"Joram, the name of three Israelites and one Syrian","kjv":"Joram","count":4,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H1568","lemma":"גִּלְעָד","xlit":"Gilʻâd","gloss":"Gilad, a region East of the Jordan","kjv":"Gilead, Gileadite","count":5,"share":0.19}],"verses":["1Kgs.22.3","1Kgs.22.29","2Kgs.8.28","2Kgs.9.1","2Kgs.9.4","2Kgs.9.14","2Chr.22.5","Deut.4